{
  "brand": "fig-and-bloom",
  "version": "3.6.2",
  "system": "Lust + Cervanttis + Neuzeit Grotesk on white / ink / clay-tint #ECE6DF / clay #D8CCBE. v3 adds the seed lanes (from the 2023 PSD kit, reconciled to this palette) and asset-library photo queries. v3.2 makes every story lane truly multi-ratio (relational layout, all four ratios) and builds out the Good Weekend editorial set (feature / pullquote / column / press / linkout). v3.4 expands carousel-journal into a full editorial blog carousel: new statement / quote / photo-statement slide types (theme levers clay|dark|light), an editorial cover layout, an author-card closing, and automatic NN/NN pagination on the body slides. v3.5 adds the editorial-standard emphasis: a scarce _turn-word_ inline marker that sets the word in italic Lust across the editorial lanes (carousel-journal, story-editorial); Cervanttis stays an accent/voice face, never inline. font-synthesis:none is set lane-wide (no faked bold), with a synthesised oblique for the emphasis until the licensed Lust-Italic.otf is added to fonts/. Aligns with the editorial-carousel-craft critique skill. v3.6 is a carousel-journal presentation fix: the dark closing sign-off becomes the hero — the Cervanttis voice line is ~2x larger and optically centred over the plate (foot logo top, CTA pill + URL at the foot retained), filling the dead space the small top-anchored line left. Presentation-only; no token, lever or enum changes. v3.6.1 fixes lever delivery: a slide's levers (cover theme/layout, statement/quote theme, …) are now honoured whether a client puts them inside `tokens` or in a sibling `levers` object — the renderer and validator merge both. Previously a separate `levers` object was dropped, so cover `theme:\"dark\"` silently fell back to `light` (black type, no scrim) and `layout:\"editorial\"` fell back to `masthead`. v3.6.2 makes the Cervanttis (script) role descender-safe by construction: Cervanttis descends ~0.806em below the baseline (far past its ~1.2 line-box), so a descender (j g y p q) on a script line stacked above other copy — card-note `line` over `sub`, the `voice` line over the headline on the story/journal lanes — dropped out of its line-box and onto the block beneath (the render still reported `overflow:false`; the glyph overflows its own line, not the card). Each such script line now reserves the descender overflow (`--cerv-descent-clear:0.29em`, em-relative so it holds at every ratio) as padding below the block, honouring the system's Cervanttis rule ('its own line, with breathing room below'). Presentation-only; no token, lever or enum changes. A new pixel-accurate check (`test/descender-intrusion.js`, `npm run test:descender`) guards the class the `overflow` check silently passed. See design-system/SYSTEM.md.",
